course: dictionary
lesson: 8817
title: One word, many shelves
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A word can mean different things in different places. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning to use. Look for clues like «wall», «cupboard», «library» or «ice».
explain: «She picks it up and puts it high on a shelf before he can reach it.» The clues are high and reach. A shelf is a flat board you put things on, so the marble sits on a board, up out of a baby's reach.
explain: «Chocolate... stays hard on a cool shelf.» In a shop or a kitchen, a shelf is a place for things to sit. Now try the meaning in the sentence: "stays hard on a cool flat board" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Shelf is a noun with a plural: one shelf, two «shelves». When you meet a new meaning, such as an ice shelf or «on the shelf», read the words around it, and check a dictionary if you are still not sure.
fact: A shelf is a flat board on a wall or in a cupboard for putting things on.
fact: The plural of shelf is shelves.
fact: A shelf can also be a flat layer of rock or ice, as in «ice shelf».
fact: «On the shelf» means put aside and not used.
fact: In shops and libraries, «top shelf» and «bottom shelf» tell you where things are, and the library catalogue shows which shelf each book is on.
exercise: «She put the marble high on a shelf before her baby brother could reach it.» Where did the marble go? | On the floor under the rug | In the bin | *On a flat board for putting things on | Down a hole in the wall
exercise: In «ice shelf», what does shelf mean? | A cold drink kept in a freezer | A ring worn on a finger | A bag for shopping | *A flat layer of ice
exercise: Mum says, «The idea is on the shelf for now.» What does «on the shelf» mean? | A plate sitting on a wall | Stacked very high | Left in the library for a week | *Put aside and not used for now
test: «The library catalogue shows which shelf each book is on.» What is a shelf in this sentence? | Put aside and not used | A layer of ice on a lake | A tall ladder | *A flat board for putting books on
test: «Aluminium cans can be recycled and be back on the shelf within about two months.» What does shelf mean here? | A flat shelf of rock in the sea | Put aside and never used | A ledge on a cliff face | *A place in a shop where goods are put for sale
exam: What is the plural of shelf? | shelfs | *shelves | shelvs | shelfes
